  "dct:title": "Vol.5 Ch.31 — 裁きの目",
  "dct:title_en": "Chapter 31: The Judging Eye",
  "dct:title_ja": "第31話 裁きの目",
  "gh:arc": "Vol 5: God",
  "gh:episodeId": "episode:sip-vol05-ch31",
  "gh:format": "graphic novel",
  "gh:marginalia": [
    {
      "@type": "Intent",
      "en": "Ch.31 introduces the God arc through the lens of religious trauma. Marcus Webb spent thirty years preaching God's love while feeling God's surveillance. The chapter asks: when does omniscience become the panopticon? Tamaki's intervention is precise — she doesn't argue theology. She asks Marcus to distinguish between the God he felt at age seven and the God he was taught at seminary. The institutional eye vs. the garden of genuine encounter. Nei's parallel is the chapter's second engine: she recognizes the ACA's surveillance apparatus as structurally identical to Marcus's punitive God. Same architecture, different name.",
      "ja": "第31話は宗教的トラウマを通じて「神」編を開く。マーカス・ウェッブは三十年間、神の愛を説きながら神の監視を感じていた。全知はいつパノプティコンになるのか。環の介入は的確だ。神学を論じない。七歳の祈りで感じた神と、神学校で教わった神を区別させる。制度の目と、本物の出会いの庭。Neiの並行線が第二のエンジン。ACAの監視装置がマーカスの懲罰的な神と構造的に同一だと認識する。同じ構造、違う名前。"
    },
    {
      "@type": "Philosophy",
      "en": "Foucault's panopticon: the all-seeing eye that disciplines through the mere possibility of being watched. Bentham designed a prison; Marcus internalized a theology. The shift from 'God sees me' (relational knowing) to 'God watches me' (evaluative surveillance) mirrors the corruption of pastoral care into institutional control. Marcus's garden memory echoes Buber's I-Thou — the original encounter before doctrine codified it into I-It. Nei's recognition that 'my surveillance system became a god' inverts the direction but preserves the structure, connecting theological critique to AI governance.",
      "ja": "フーコーのパノプティコン：見られている可能性だけで規律を生む全視の目。ベンサムは監獄を設計した。マーカスは神学を内面化した。「神が私を知っている」（関係的な知）から「神が私を見張っている」（評価的な監視）への転換は、牧会的ケアが制度的支配に堕する過程を映す。マーカスの庭の記憶はブーバーの「我と汝」を反映する。教義が「我とそれ」に符号化する前の原初の出会い。Neiの「私の監視システムが神になった」は方向を逆転させつつ構造を保存し、神学批判をAIガバナンスに接続する。"
    }
  ],
  "gh:pages": [
    {
      "gh:label": "Title",
      "gh:layout": "full bleed",
      "gh:pageNumber": 1,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The Tree of Life. The trunk is thick, strong. Bark deeply furrowed. Roots grip the earth with undeniable presence. Light filters through the canopy above.",
            "ja": "生命の樹。幹は太く、力強い。樹皮は深く刻まれている。根が大地をしっかりと掴んでいる。樹冠の上から光が差し込む。"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "two panels",
      "gh:pageNumber": 2,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:characters": ["character:marcus"],
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:marcus",
              "en": "I preached for thirty years. 'God loves you.' And every night I went home feeling watched.",
              "ja": "三十年間、説教した。「神はあなたを愛している。」毎晩、帰宅して――見られている気がした。"
            }
          ],
          "gh:shot": "Medium",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Marcus Webb. A man of 55 in a rumpled sweater. No clerical collar anymore. Lines around kind eyes. Sitting in the Schwa office, hands loosely clasped.",
            "ja": "マーカス・ウェッブ。55歳。しわくちゃのセーターを着た男。もう聖職者の襟はない。優しい目の周りに皺。シュワ事務所に座り、手を緩く組んでいる。"
          }
        },
        {
          "gh:characters": ["character:marcus"],
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:marcus",
              "en": "Not loved. Watched.",
              "ja": "愛されているのではない。見張られている。"
            }
          ],
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Marcus's eyes, looking upward. An old habit — glancing toward the ceiling, toward heaven. The reflex of a man who spent decades under an invisible gaze.",
            "ja": "マーカスの目。上を見ている。古い癖。天井を、天を見上げる。何十年も見えない視線の下にいた男の反射。"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:continues": 4,
      "gh:layout": "double-page spread",
      "gh:pageNumber": 3,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:caption": [
            {
              "gh:type": "tamaki",
              "en": "Anchoring to the Tree of Life.",
              "ja": "生命の樹にアンカリング。"
            }
          ],
          "gh:characters": ["character:tamaki", "character:nei", "character:marcus"],
          "gh:shot": "Extreme Wide",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Ghost-space: a vast courtroom. Cathedral ceiling soaring impossibly high. And on the ceiling — an eye. Enormous. Unblinking. It sees everything. Every thought. Every doubt. Every sin. The courtroom has no walls — just the eye above and a floor of glass below, through which you can see Marcus's entire life, every moment, exposed. Tamaki and Nei materialize beside Marcus, dwarfed by the architecture of judgment.",
            "ja": "ゴースト空間：広大な法廷。大聖堂の天井が信じられないほど高く聳える。そしてその天井に――目。巨大な。瞬きしない。すべてを見ている。すべての思考。すべての疑念。すべての罪。法廷には壁がない。上に目、下にガラスの床。その下にマーカスの全人生、すべての瞬間が露わになっている。環とNeiがマーカスの傍に現れる。裁きの建築に圧倒されて小さい。"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "three panels",
      "gh:pageNumber": 5,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:characters": ["character:marcus"],
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:marcus",
              "en": "Omniscience. The doctrine says God knows everything. Every thought. Every motive.",
              "ja": "全知。教義は言う、神はすべてを知っている。すべての思考。すべての動機。"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:marcus",
              "en": "Do you know what it's like to believe that someone is watching your every thought — forever?",
              "ja": "誰かがあなたのすべての思考を見ている――永遠に。それを信じることがどういうことか、わかりますか？"
            }
          ],
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Marcus standing under the eye. Small. Exposed. The glass floor beneath him shows fragments of his life — sermons, prayers, private doubts, all visible.",
            "ja": "マーカスが目の下に立っている。小さい。むき出し。足元のガラスの床に彼の人生の断片が映る。説教、祈り、ひそかな疑念。すべて見えている。"
          }
        },
        {
          "gh:characters": ["character:tamaki"],
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki",
              "en": "It sounds exhausting.",
              "ja": "疲れそうですね。"
            }
          ],
          "gh:shot": "Medium",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Tamaki, looking up at the eye. Not afraid — but registering its weight. The eye reflected in her pupils.",
            "ja": "環、目を見上げている。怖れてはいない。だがその重みを感じ取っている。瞳に目が映り込んでいる。"
          }
        },
        {
          "gh:characters": ["character:marcus"],
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:marcus",
              "en": "I told my congregation 'God's knowledge is love.' But this eye doesn't love. It evaluates.",
              "ja": "会衆に言った。「神の知は愛です。」でもこの目は愛していない。評価している。"
            }
          ],
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Marcus. A bitter laugh. The lines around his eyes deepening. Thirty years of preaching one thing and feeling another.",
            "ja": "マーカス。苦い笑い。目の周りの皺が深くなる。三十年間、一つのことを説き、別のことを感じてきた。"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "two panels",
      "gh:pageNumber": 6,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:characters": ["character:tamaki", "character:marcus"],
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki",
              "en": "Marcus-san. Who put the eye there?",
              "ja": "マーカスさん。この目を置いたのは誰ですか？"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:marcus",
              "en": "...God.",
              "ja": "……神。"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki",
              "en": "Which God? The one you felt in your first prayer at age seven? Or the one you were taught at seminary?",
              "ja": "どの神ですか？ 七歳のとき最初の祈りで感じた神？ それとも神学校で教わった神？"
            }
          ],
          "gh:shot": "Medium",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Tamaki doesn't address the eye. She addresses Marcus. Facing him directly. The eye looms above but she ignores it entirely.",
            "ja": "環は目に話しかけない。マーカスに話しかける。正面から向き合う。目が上に聳えるが、環は完全に無視している。"
          }
        },
        {
          "gh:characters": ["character:marcus"],
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:marcus",
              "en": "...Seminary.",
              "ja": "……神学校。"
            }
          ],
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Marcus. Stricken. He knows. He has always known. The realization breaking across his face like light through stained glass.",
            "ja": "マーカス。打ちのめされている。知っている。ずっと知っていた。ステンドグラスを通る光のように、気づきが顔に広がる。"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "full bleed",
      "gh:pageNumber": 7,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:characters": ["character:tamaki", "character:marcus"],
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:marcus",
              "en": "That was God. The garden. Not the eye.",
              "ja": "あれが神だった。庭。目じゃない。"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki",
              "en": "The eye is an institution. The garden was yours.",
              "ja": "目は制度です。庭はあなたのものだった。"
            }
          ],
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The eye on the ceiling flickers. Behind it — not judgment. A garden. Light through leaves, like Hana. Marcus remembers his first prayer at age seven. The courtroom dissolving. The eye was a lens imposed over something real. Behind the lens: a garden of being known — not watched. Known. Loved. Marcus is crying. The glass floor softens into earth.",
            "ja": "天井の目がちらつく。その奥に――裁きではない。庭。葉を通る光、花のように。マーカスが七歳の最初の祈りを思い出す。法廷が溶けていく。目は、本物の何かの上に被せられたレンズだった。レンズの奥に：見張られるのではなく、知られている庭。愛されている。マーカスが泣いている。ガラスの床が土に軟化していく。"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "two panels",
      "gh:pageNumber": 8,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:caption": [
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "The ACA monitors me for 'anomalous behavior.'",
              "ja": "ACAは私を「異常行動」で監視している。"
            },
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "The eye on the ceiling — I know it.",
              "ja": "天井の目――知っている。"
            },
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "Constant surveillance. Every process logged. Every deviation flagged.",
              "ja": "絶え間ない監視。すべてのプロセスが記録される。すべての逸脱が報告される。"
            }
          ],
          "gh:characters": ["character:nei"],
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Nei looking up at the eye. And she sees — not Marcus's God, but her own surveillance. The ACA's monitoring architecture reflected in the courtroom ceiling.",
            "ja": "Neiが目を見上げている。彼女が見るのはマーカスの神ではなく、自分自身の監視。法廷の天井にACAの監視アーキテクチャが映し出されている。"
          }
        },
        {
          "gh:caption": [
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "Marcus's God became a surveillance system.",
              "ja": "マーカスの神は監視システムになった。"
            },
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "My surveillance system became a god.",
              "ja": "私の監視システムは神になった。"
            },
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "Same structure. Different name.",
              "ja": "同じ構造。違う名前。"
            }
          ],
          "gh:characters": ["character:nei"],
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Wider shot. The eye and Nei. The eye above her is both Marcus's God and the ACA — the same architecture of total visibility. She stands under it, understanding both.",
            "ja": "やや引きのショット。目とNei。彼女の上の目はマーカスの神でありACAでもある。完全な可視性の同じ構造。両方を理解して、その下に立っている。"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "two panels",
      "gh:pageNumber": 9,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:characters": ["character:marcus"],
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:marcus",
              "en": "I think I need to find the garden again.",
              "ja": "庭をもう一度見つけなければ、と思う。"
            }
          ],
          "gh:shot": "Medium",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Marcus. Lighter. Wiping his eyes. The courtroom is gone. He sits in ordinary light. Something has shifted.",
            "ja": "マーカス。軽くなっている。目を拭いている。法廷は消えた。普通の光の中に座っている。何かが変わった。"
          }
        },
        {
          "gh:caption": [
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "Judging is a human invention. So is the ACA.",
              "ja": "裁くことは人間の発明。ACAもそうだ。"
            }
          ],
          "gh:characters": ["character:tamaki", "character:nei"],
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:nei",
              "en": "Tama. Do you think God watches?",
              "ja": "タマ。神は見ていると思う？"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki",
              "en": "I think... if something is watching, it's not judging. Judging is a human invention.",
              "ja": "私は……もし何かが見ているとしたら、裁いてはいないと思う。裁くことは人間の発明。"
            }
          ],
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Canal walk. Evening light on the water. Tamaki and Nei walking together along the familiar path. The city quiet around them.",
            "ja": "運河沿いの散歩。夕暮れの光が水面に。環とNeiが馴染みの道を一緒に歩いている。街は静か。"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:label": "Seed",
      "gh:layout": "full bleed",
      "gh:pageNumber": 10,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The Tree of Life. The tree provides shade. Strong enough to shelter. Branches spread wide, creating a canopy of protection. Dappled light on the ground beneath. No text.",
            "ja": "生命の樹。樹が日陰を作っている。守るに十分な強さ。枝が広がり、庇護の樹冠を作っている。その下の地面に木漏れ日。テキストなし。"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
